{sov: Notes}
Andalusian Cadence: Driven entirely by a classic 2-bar descending minor
walkdown (i - VII - VI - V7) looping in A minor throughout the song.

Call and Response: The structure features Ray Charles' lead vocals
answering tight, syncopated backing vocals from the Raelettes.

Rhythm Comping: Emphasize the driving quarter-note walkdown in the bass/keys.
Guitarists can accent the offbeats with short, sharp stabs on upper triads.

Turnaround Tension: The landing on E7 provides the dominant push back
to Am, often incorporating an G# leading tone in lead solos.
{eov}